+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop on Lantern Row in Oakfield. It has four pages:
+
+- **Home** (`index.html`): introduction, staff picks, the next event and a visit teaser.
+- **Books** (`books.html`): a catalogue of 15 titles in six genres. A genre filter updates the list and the address bar (for example `books.html?genre=mystery`), so filtered views can be bookmarked and shared.
+- **Events** (`events.html`): upcoming readings, workshops and book groups with dates and times.
+- **Visit** (`visit.html`): opening hours, the shop address and a contact form. The form is a demo and does not send messages.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step, no framework and no external request of any kind: no CDNs, web fonts, analytics or map embeds.
+
+## Run it locally
+
+Any static file server will do. From the repository root, run one of:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8080
+```
+
+```sh
+npx http-server . -p 8080
+```
+
+Then open <http://localhost:8080/>.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+The tests load each page in headless Google Chrome through the globally installed Playwright, and start their own static server on a random free port. They need Node 22 or later, Playwright and Chrome at `/usr/bin/google-chrome`.
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node --test tests/*.test.js
+```
+
+To run one file, pass its path, for example `NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node --test tests/books.test.js`.
+
+To check the syntax of every script:
+
+```sh
+for f in js/*.js; do node --check "$f" || exit 1; done
+```
+
+## Layout
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: pages, each with the shared header, navigation and footer.
+- `css/styles.css`: shared styles.
+- `js/books-data.js`: the book catalogue. `js/books.js` renders and filters it. `js/visit.js` validates the contact form.
+- `favicon.svg`: the site icon.
+- `tests/`: Playwright tests, one file per concern.
+- `FEATURE_FLOW.md`: the project's checks and conventions.
