+      </ul>
+    </nav>
+  </header>
+
+  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
+    <h1>Events</h1>
+    <p>Readings, workshops and book groups in the shop and on Lantern Row. Everything is free unless the listing says otherwise, and seats are first come, first served.</p>
+    <p>Evening events are held after hours: we reopen the door at the start time shown for each one. The shop closes at 7:00pm on Thursdays and 5:00pm on Saturdays; see <a href="visit.html">opening hours</a>.</p>
+
+    <ul class="card-list">
+      <li class="card">
+        <h2>Winter poetry open mic</h2>
+        <p class="event-when"><time datetime="2026-12-03T18:30">Thursday 3 December 2026, 6:30pm</time></p>
+        <p>Three minutes each, no sign-up needed before the doors open. Read your own work or a favourite poem. Hot drinks are served from the back counter.</p>
+      </li>
+      <li class="card">
+        <h2>Saturday storytime</h2>
+        <p class="event-when"><time datetime="2026-12-12T11:00">Saturday 12 December 2026, 11:00am</time></p>
+        <p>Picture books and a little percussion for children aged three to six. Grown-ups welcome, and there is a reading corner with cushions by the window.</p>
+      </li>
+      <li class="card">
+        <h2>Book club: The Glass Orchard</h2>
+        <p class="event-when"><time datetime="2027-01-14T19:00">Thursday 14 January 2027, 7:00pm</time></p>
+        <p>We discuss the January pick over a glass of cider. Copies are available from the shop, and the group is friendly to people who did not finish the book.</p>
+      </li>
+      <li class="card">
+        <h2>Letterpress card workshop</h2>
+        <p class="event-when"><time datetime="2027-02-06T10:00">Saturday 6 February 2027, 10:00am</time></p>
+        <p>Set type by hand and print a pair of greeting cards on our Albion press. The workshop takes about two hours and all materials are provided. Places are limited to eight.</p>
+      </li>
+      <li class="card">
+        <h2>Author talk: Helen Achterberg</h2>
+        <p class="event-when"><time datetime="2027-03-20T19:30">Saturday 20 March 2027, 7:30pm</time></p>
+        <p>The poet talks about writing Low Tide Sonnets on the strand at Halsey, followed by questions and a signing. Please arrive by 7:15pm to find a seat.</p>
+      </li>
+    </ul>
+  </main>
+
+  <footer class="site-footer">
+    <p>Marginalia Books, 14 Lantern Row, Oakfield. Independent since 1987.</p>
+    <p>&copy; 2026 Marginalia Books</p>
+  </footer>
+</body>
+</html>
